### The Fragile Base Class Problem

The primary danger of inheritance is the **Fragile Base Class** problem: changes to superclass implementation details silently ripple down and corrupt subclass behavior.

Because inheritance exposes internal superclass mechanics to subclasses, it breaks encapsulation across class boundaries.

**Why Composition is Superior to Inheritance in Most Scenarios:**
1. **Preserves Encapsulation**: With composition, the enclosing class interacts with component objects exclusively through their public API.
2. **Runtime Flexibility**: Internal components can be dynamically swapped at runtime via setters or dependency injection.
3. **Avoids Class Explosion**: Instead of creating dozens of rigid subclasses (`FlyingSwimmingAnimal`, `FlyingNoSwimmingAnimal`), you compose distinct capabilities.

---

### Solving Fragile Inheritance with Forwarding Wrappers (Composition)

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

// Component interface
interface DataLogger {
    void log(String entry);
}

class ConsoleLogger implements DataLogger {
    @Override
    public void log(String entry) {
        System.out.println("[CONSOLE LOG] " + entry);
    }
}

// Composition-based wrapper: holds a reference instead of extending
class SecureAuditLogger implements DataLogger {
    private final DataLogger targetLogger; // Composition reference

    public SecureAuditLogger(DataLogger targetLogger) {
        this.targetLogger = targetLogger;
    }

    @Override
    public void log(String entry) {
        // Adds security augmentation and forwards cleanly
        System.out.print("[AUDIT HASH: " + Integer.toHexString(entry.hashCode()) + "] ");
        targetLogger.log(entry);
    }
}

public class CompositionOverInheritanceDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        DataLogger base = new ConsoleLogger();
        DataLogger secure = new SecureAuditLogger(base);

        secure.log("User authentication initiated");
    }
}
```

**Console Output:**
```text
[AUDIT HASH: 66c303f2] [CONSOLE LOG] User authentication initiated
```

---

### The Golden Rule of OOP Design

Favor composition over inheritance. Use inheritance only when a true, immutable IS-A relationship exists and the subclass is 100% substitutable for the superclass without side effects.

